{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1372592-fiction-discussion-dragon-blooded-novella-the-silence-of-our-ancestors","id":1372592,"title":"[Fiction Discussion] Dragon-Blooded Novella, \"The Silence of Our Ancestors\"","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Dragon-Blooded"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-03-03T18:19:56-08:00","id":1372592,"title":"[Fiction Discussion] Dragon-Blooded Novella, \"The Silence of Our Ancestors\"","content":"I just finished reading this, and I wanted to start talking about this. Obviously, the thread will have spoilers.<br /> <br /> I must say, I <i>really</i> liked this one. The previous Exalted 3rd Edition fiction has left me a little cold, either because I thought the authors got the world rather wrong, because the prose just wasn't all that inspiring, or a bit of both. But The Silence of Our Ancestors really knocked it out of the park for me on both those fronts. All the supernatural stuff made sense in terms of the world, but didn't feel like I was just reading a statblock, if that makes sense. And the characters were engaging and well-written, with distinct personalities and voices. I want to hear more about their adventures! Also, be sure to read the epilogue, it has some interesting information in it. :-)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},